WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
How to actually pass this class

2
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.920
How is the grade built?

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:24.560
80% exams, 20% problem sets, plus up to 3% extra credit from Top Hat. Your best exam counts 30%, the other two 25% each — or swap Midterm 3 for a comprehensive final worth 40% if it helps.

4
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.220
What quietly protects you in the syllabus?

5
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:39.470
Your lowest problem set is dropped (missing ones can be emailed at term’s end for 50%), and about five classes of Top Hat are excused. But no pset extensions, ever.

6
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:43.760
Step 1 of the four-step method?

7
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:54.100
Review each slide deck right after lecture, ruthlessly: could you explain every point to a friend, out loud, with no notes? He says 95% of students fool themselves here.

8
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.900
Step 2 and 3?

9
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:12.300
Do the psets alone first — every problem targets one building block, so ask which concept it is testing. Then friend, then TA. Then read the answer key carefully, including for questions you got right: a right answer for the wrong reason still costs you.

10
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.620
Step 4, and the thing he asks you to do yourself?

11
00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:29.660
Practice exams, timed and closed-note — then modify every question. What would make a different answer correct? Can you reverse it Jeopardy-style? He asks you to do this rep yourself rather than having AI generate questions for you.

12
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.680
What separates A students?

13
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:43.740
Memorizers do fine until a question asks them to do something new with a definition. Top grades go to students who learned the connections between building blocks, not just the blocks.

14
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.000
How to actually pass this class — 6 cards
